(3.5    Training Objective and Optimization) Tj
T*
(The SAE is trained to minimize reconstruction error subject to sparsity in the latent code. For each) Tj
T*
(activation vector ai , the loss is) Tj
T*
(                                   L\(ai \) = ||ai - ?i ||22 + lambda||zi ||1 ,                            \(8\)) Tj
T*
(where lambda > 0 controls the sparsity-fidelity trade-off. Optimization is performed using mini-batch) Tj
T*
(gradient descent over the activation dataset H.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.6    Ranking Tokens for a Learned Feature) Tj
T*
(After training, learned features are interpreted by identifying the tokens that most strongly activate a) Tj
T*
(given feature. Let zi,j denote the activation of feature j on token i. For each feature j, we rank tokens) Tj
T*
(by zi,j and inspect the top-K items:) Tj
T*
(                                                           K) Tj
T*
(                                     TopK\(j\) = arg        max         zi,j .                          \(9\)) Tj
T*
(                                                       iin{1,...,N }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The decoded token and its associated context are recorded for each selected index, enabling qualitative) Tj
T*
(assessment of whether feature j corresponds to a coherent semantic pattern.) Tj
