(   5     Advantages and Limitations) Tj
T*
(   5.1    Advantages) Tj
T*
(   Large language models are trained almost entirely through text, and their internal representations are) Tj
T*
(   thus shaped primarily by textual regularities and abstractions. Feature-based interpretability methods) Tj
T*
(   that operate directly on token-level activations align well with this mode of learning.) Tj
T*
(       GPT-2 was used as the base model as it offered activation extraction without excess computa-) Tj
T*
(   tional cost, and despite its smaller scale, allowed for the scaling down of the implementation without) Tj
T*
(   inconvenience.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5.2    Limitations) Tj
T*
(   A fundamental limitation of monosemanticity is that the presence of interpretable features does not) Tj
T*
(   guarantee reliable insight into a model's internal objectives. Moreover, monosemantic representations) Tj
T*
(   are learned with respect to observed activations and training data distributions. Features that appear) Tj
T*
(   benign or coherent under typical inputs may behave differently under distributional shift or adversarial) Tj
T*
(   prompting. Additionally, the assumption that internal representations can be cleanly decomposed into) Tj
T*
(   sparse, human-aligned features may not hold uniformly across all layers or models. [5]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   6     Conclusion) Tj
T*
(   This work explores sparse autoencoder-based dictionary learning as a tool formechanistic interpretabil-) Tj
T*
(   ity in transformer language models. By applying this method to GPT-2 activations, it is possible to) Tj
T*
(   recover interpretable, sparse features that correspond to coherent semantic concepts.) Tj
T*
(       These findings support the broader view that language models encode meaning in distributed) Tj
T*
(   activation patterns rather than individual neurons. While the present experiments are limited in) Tj
T*
(   scale, they reproduce key aspects of prior work. Future work could extend this approach to multiple) Tj
T*
(   layers, larger datasets, cross-domain corpora,and even automated methods for feature labeling and) Tj
T*
(   comparison.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
